7}, {\"nodes\": [58, 1116, 1450], \"t_close\": 58449, \"t_wedge_complete\": 57695}, {\"nodes\": [61, 855, 987], \"t_close\": 49814, \"t_wedge_complete\": 49640}, {\"nodes\": [65, 389, 1450], \"t_close\": 58574, \"t_wedge_complete\": 58349}, {\"nodes\": [82, 1064, 1467], \"t_close\": 57329, \"t_wedge_complete\": 56720}, {\"nodes\": [84, 754, 801], \"t_close\": 57450, \"t_wedge_complete\": 57362}], \"fraction_closed\": 0.3046, \"median_closing_lag\": 1959.0, \"n_closed_within_delta\": 106, \"n_triangles\": 348}", "latency_ms": 22, "tokens_before": 38490, "tokens_after": 38490, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_459a1eed", "decision": "present", "mechanism": "closure_wave", "entities": [39, 54, 82, 85, 115, 116, 118, 172, 188, 207, 229, 260], "window": [47332, 59332], "confidence": 0.89, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "All 10 triangles spanning the target nodes close within 800 units of their supporting wedge (fraction_closed=1.0, median lag 497), versus a graph-wide baseline of 30.5% / lag 1959 and a hub baseline of just 21.9% / lag 2447. The targets are low-degree (2-6 events) and absent from the top-activity list, ruling out volume and popularity as explanations. The same nodes yield zero triangles in the adjacent window, so the structure is time-localised rather than a static connection; and a delta=100 test yields no closures, confirming a genuine ~500-unit propagation lag. Closures span 48595-58120 across all activity bins, so this is a distributed wave rather than one burst."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Primary signal (step_02):** All 12 target nodes participate in exactly one triangle each (step_13), and **10/10 triangles closed within 800 units** of their supporting wedge completing \u2014 `fraction_closed = 1.0`, median lag **497**. Each node contributes exactly one prompt closure, a remarkably uniform pattern.\n\n**Confounder controls:**\n\n1. **Volume/popularity is not the driver (step_03, step_04).** None of the target nodes appear among the top-12 most active nodes (which range 33\u2013143 events). The targets have only 2\u20136 events and 2\u20136 distinct partners each. This is a sparse, low-degree set \u2014 closure cannot be explained by these nodes simply firing a lot of edges.\n\n2. **Prompt closure is not generic to this window (step_14).** Graph-wide, only **30.5%** of 348 triangles close within 800, median lag **1959**. The target set's 100% / 497 is a sharp departure from baseline.\n\n3. **Hubs do *not* show this behaviour (step_05).** The actual high-volume nodes generate 288 triangles but close only **21.9%** within 800, median lag **2446.5** \u2014 worse than baseline. So the effect is specific to the target set, not a byproduct of dense activity.\n\n4. **Not a static-connectivity artifact (step_06, step_07).** In the shifted control window [59333, 71333] the same nodes produce **zero** triangles, so this is time-localised rather than a permanent structural feature. At `delta = 100` nothing closes, confirming the ~497 lag is a genuine measured propagation delay, not degenerate simultaneous edges.\n\n5. **Not a single activity burst (step_10).** Activity is spread across all 8 bins (5,2,2,4,3,2,10,10) and the closures themselves span t_close 48595 \u2192 58120 \u2014 the wave is distributed over the interval, not an artifact of one dense spike. Individual closing edges verified as real single events (step_09: 229\u2192116; step_11: 85\u219239).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_459a1eed\",\n  \"decision\": \"present\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"closure_wave\",\n  \"entities\": [39, 54, 82, 85, 115, 116, 118, 172, 188, 207, 229, 260],\n  \"window\": [47332, 59332],\n  \"confidence\": 0.89,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"All 10 triangles spanning the target nodes close within 800 units of their supporting wedge (fraction_closed=1.0, median lag 497), versus a graph-wide baseline of 30.5% / lag 1959 and a hub baseline of just 21.9% / lag 2447. The targets are low-degree (2-6 events) and absent from the top-activity list, ruling out volume and popularity as explanations. The same nodes yield zero triangles in the adjacent window, so the structure is time-localised rather than a static connection; and a delta=100 test yields no closures, confirming a genuine ~500-unit propagation lag. Closures span 48595-58120 across all activity bins, so this is a distributed wave rather than one burst.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 47909, "total_output_tokens": 4389, "total_tokens": 52298, "total_latency_ms": 64569, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}